  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>The controller for personal data processed through this website is <span class="placeholder">[Oneward legal entity name]</span>, <span class="placeholder">[registered address]</span> ("Oneward", "we"). You can reach us at <a href="mailto:privacy@getoneward.com">privacy@getoneward.com</a> <span class="placeholder">[confirm mailbox]</span>. <span class="placeholder">[If a data protection officer is appointed, add name and contact here.]</span></p>

  <h2>2. What this policy covers</h2>
  <p>This policy covers personal data we process when you visit getoneward.com or contact us through it. Data we process on behalf of customers during a 30-day analysis or a deployment is governed by the agreements with that customer (NDA and data processing agreement), not by this policy. How we handle that data is described on our <a href="/trust-and-security">Trust & Security</a> page.</p>

  <h2>3. Data we collect and why</h2>
  <h3>When you request a 30-day analysis or contact us</h3>
  <p>If you submit the request form or email us, we process the information you provide: name, work email, and, if you choose to give them, company, location, company website, your current HRIS, and other HR tools you use. We use this to reply to you, to prepare the first call, and to set up the NDA and analysis you asked for.</p>
  <p>Legal basis: taking steps at your request before entering into a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and our legitimate interest in responding to business enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).</p>
  <h3>When you visit the site</h3>
  <p>Our hosting provider records technical access data, such as your IP address, browser type, the pages requested, and the time of the request, in server logs for security and to keep the site running. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in operating a secure website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). <span class="placeholder">[Name hosting provider and log retention period.]</span></p>
  <p>This website does not use analytics, advertising, or tracking cookies. See the <a href="/cookie-notice">Cookie Notice</a>.</p>

  <h2>4. Who receives your data</h2>
  <p>We share personal data only with service providers that help us run the website and handle enquiries, under contracts that restrict what they may do with it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Hosting and content delivery <span class="placeholder">[provider, location]</span></li>
    <li>Email and calendar tools used to reply to you and schedule calls <span class="placeholder">[providers]</span></li>
    <li>Scheduling: if you book a demo call, Calendly processes the booking under its own privacy policy.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal data and do not share it with third parties for their own marketing.</p>

  <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Oneward processes data in the EU. Where a service provider processes data outside the EU or EEA, we rely on an adequacy decision or the European Commission's standard contractual clauses, with additional safeguards where needed. <span class="placeholder">[Confirm for each provider listed above.]</span></p>

  <h2>6. How long we keep data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Enquiry and request data: for as long as needed to handle your enquiry, and then for up to <span class="placeholder">[12 months]</span> unless a contract follows, in which case retention follows that contract.</li>
    <li>Server logs: <span class="placeholder">[retention period]</span>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We keep data longer only where a legal obligation requires it.</p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to access your personal data, to have it corrected or erased, to restrict or object to its processing, and to receive it in a portable format. Where processing is based on legitimate interest, you may object at any time on grounds relating to your situation. To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:privacy@getoneward.com">privacy@getoneward.com</a>.</p>
  <p>You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, in particular in the EU member state of your residence, workplace, or the place of the alleged infringement. <span class="placeholder">[Name the competent authority for Oneward's establishment, e.g. the Hessian Commissioner for Data Protection if established in Frankfurt.]</span></p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>We protect personal data with technical and organisational measures appropriate to the risk, including encryption in transit, access controls, and least-privilege access for our staff. Our approach to customer data is described on the <a href="/trust-and-security">Trust & Security</a> page.</p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>This website is aimed at businesses and is not intended for anyone under 16. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We will update this policy when our practices or the law change. The date at the top shows the latest version. Material changes will be highlighted on this page.</p>
</LegalPage>
